{"name":"Arrow Quiver","hex":"#c7a998","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"arrow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A projectile consisting of a shaft, a point and a tail with stabilizing fins that is shot from a bow.","A sign or symbol used to indicate a direction (e.g.→)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move swiftly and directly (like an arrow).","To let fly swiftly and directly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/arrow"},{"term":"quiver","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A container for arrows, crossbow bolts or darts, such as those fired from a bow, crossbow or blowgun.","A ready storage location for figurative tools or weapons."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Nimble, active."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/quiver"}],"entries":[{"title":"Arrow","blocks":[{"text":"An arrow is a fin-stabilized projectile launched by a bow. A typical arrow usually consists of a long, stiff, straight shaft with a weighty arrowhead attached to the front end, multiple fin-like stabilizers called fletchings mounted near the rear, and a slot at the rear end called a nock for engaging the bowstring. A container or bag carrying additional arrows for convenient reloading is called a quiver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/DFRArrow.jpg/330px-DFRArrow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrow"},{"title":"Quiver","blocks":[{"text":"A quiver is a container for holding arrows or bolts. It can be carried on an archer's body, the bow, or the ground, depending on the type of shooting and the archer's personal preference. Quivers were traditionally made of leather, wood, furs, and other natural materials, but are now often made of metal or plastic."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Wenceslas_Hollar_-_Quivers_and_hunting_horns.jpg/330px-Wenceslas_Hollar_-_Quivers_and_hunting_horns.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quiver"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Two_arrows.jpg/500px-Two_arrows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Two_arrows.jpg/1280px-Two_arrows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Two_arrows.jpg/500px-Two_arrows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traditional target arrow (top) and replica medieval arrow (bottom)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwo_arrows.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Warring_States_Bronze_Arrowheads.jpg/500px-Warring_States_Bronze_Arrowheads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Warring_States_Bronze_Arrowheads.jpg/1280px-Warring_States_Bronze_Arrowheads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Warring_States_Bronze_Arrowheads.jpg/500px-Warring_States_Bronze_Arrowheads.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Warring States bronze arrowheads","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWarring_States_Bronze_Arrowheads.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Bow_and_Arrow.jpg/500px-Bow_and_Arrow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Bow_and_Arrow.jpg/500px-Bow_and_Arrow.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"African bow and arrows in a quiver","link":"https://en.wik